# NOTICE

agent-governance is the framework-neutral governance core, consolidated into
this repository (owner decision 2026-08-17: single repo, single license
Apache-2.0). Extraction provenance (from the pre-consolidation standalone
repository, history bundled at backups/agent-governance-pre-consolidation.bundle):

- `packages/contracts/src/agent-interfaces.ts` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/agent-runtime/interfaces/index.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229), with `ReleaseExecutionSnapshotV1`,
  `CandidateIsolationBinding`, `Sha256Digest`, `AIRuntimeCapability` and the
  `LlmProviderConfig` structural shape inlined to keep the package
  dependency-free.
- `packages/contracts/src/runtime-boundary-ports.ts` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/agent-runtime/contracts/runtime-boundary-ports.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229), import path adapted for this repository.
- `packages/governor/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/governor-limit/**`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229); the Nest decorator and unused logger were
  removed for framework neutrality. The Nest/GraphQL interceptor stays in the
  product (future `@agent-governance/nest` package).
- `packages/outbox/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/outbox/**` and
  `packages/backend/src/common/contracts/outbox-event.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229); Nest decorators/injection and the
  observability span decorator were removed; the trace context is sourced
  from an injectable provider (default fails closed), and the
  pg_notify/BullMQ bridge is behind `OutboxNotifyTransport` (PG NOTIFY
  default, in-memory for tests). Worker/listener/cleanup (delivery side)
  stays in the product for a follow-up extraction.
- `packages/audit-chain/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/agent-runtime/entities/{agent-execution,react-step,tool-call-record}.entity.ts`,
  `…/tool-framework/tool-call-lifecycle.service.ts`,
  `…/executor/execution-state-machine.ts`,
  `packages/backend/src/common/security/{redact-sensitive-payload,apply-json-redaction-pointers}.ts`
  and the canonical helpers of `shared/agent-executable-assets`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229). GraphQL decorators and the Agent relation
  were stripped (presentation stays product-side); Nest injection removed
  (constructor takes the repository); product executable-assets types are
  structural stand-ins; `CandidateIsolationBinding.isolationSnapshotHash`
  was added to the inlined contracts type to match the product shape.
- `packages/permission/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/agent-permission/**` and the
  `getAllowedTools` resolution of
  `packages/backend/src/modules/agent-runtime/context-builder/context-builder.service.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229). SEMANTIC FIX: the product's empty allow-list
  meant "no restriction" because the context builder always injected 6
  hardcoded CRM defaults; the standalone package inverts this — empty
  allow-list denies unless `allowEmptyList: true`, and `resolveAllowedTools`
  defaults to no tools instead of the legacy CRM default set. Nest
  decorators/HttpException replaced with plain classes/Errors.
- `packages/guardrail/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/guardrail/services/{rule-matcher,risk-assessor,guardrail-engine}.service.ts`,
  `…/interfaces/index.ts` and the guardrail rule/log entities
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229). Nest decorators/injection removed; rule
  loading (TypeORM + Redis cache) is behind `RuleProvider` with in-memory and
  TypeORM implementations. The action actuator (EventEmitter2 + approval
  port), audit logger/query, rule config and learning owners stay in the
  product for a follow-up extraction.
- `packages/approval/src/**` — derived from
  `packages/backend/src/modules/approval/entities/{approval-instance,approval-step,approval-process,approval-policy-revision}.entity.ts`
  and the decision-core slice of
  `packages/backend/src/modules/approval/services/approval-engine.service.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229): createAgentApproval / processDecision /
  processTimeout / getAuditTrail / step configuration and the CAS
  first-writer save. Nest injection, EventEmitter2, the guardrail audit
  logger and queue-membership checks are behind ports (events/audit/
  approver-check) with no-op and exact-match defaults. AI agent steps
  (model router), risk-assessment internals, policy human resolver and the
  v2 subject lifecycle stay product-side for a follow-up extraction.
  Column types were made explicit and a redundant duplicate index removed
  (the product uses hand-written migrations, so synchronize never exposed
  the collision).
- `packages/executor/src/**` — the governed ReAct loop, written as the
  convergence of the extracted packages (contracts / audit-chain / approval /
  guardrail / permission / outbox). It mirrors the governance flow of
  `nexusclaw-core`'s `agent-runtime/executor/executor-engine.service.ts`
  (nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229): deny-by-default tool gate, L0–L4 guardrail
  evaluation, L2/L3 approval pause with `guardrail_pending` + outbox paused
  event, one-shot approved-tool resume with history rebuild, and the
  execution/step/tool-call/outbox audit chain. The product's learning loop,
  model routing, cognition and prompt machinery are deliberately not part of
  this package.
- `packages/sidecar/src/**` — HTTP surface and mini console over the
  extracted packages (new code, mirroring the NexusClaw community console
  pattern); the deterministic scenario model and demo tools follow the
  governance flow verified in nexusclaw-core @ 9c10c229. The per-call
  governance gate (gate.ts + /gate routes) extends the same audit chain to
  external frameworks. No auth (local demo); the enterprise surface lives in
  the product.
- `adapters/python/**` — new code (PR-14): stdlib-only client with
  wrap_tool / run_approved over the sidecar gate API. n8n and Dify adapters
  are documented follow-ups (adapters/README.md).

